Data
----
The S1 items (governance/evals/jev-calibration/items-v1.jsonl) and the S1 run
records (results/) contain text derived from CUAD v1, the Contract Understanding
Atticus Dataset:

  CUAD v1, (c) The Atticus Project, Inc.
  Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Dataset: https://www.atticusprojectai.org/cuad
  Record:  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4595826
  Paper:   Dan Hendrycks, Collin Burns, Anya Chen and Spencer Ball.
           "CUAD: An Expert-Annotated NLP Dataset for Legal Contract Review."
           arXiv:2103.06268 (2021).

Changes made to CUAD (as CC BY 4.0 requires us to indicate):
  - Contract passages were cut to windows of at most 300 words centred on an
    annotated span; "no" items use a window from a contract that has no span of
    the queried clause type. Windows that literally name the clause type were
    excluded.
  - Each window is paired with a templated question written by NXTG.AI
    (a yes/no "does this passage contain a <clause type> clause?" question, or a
    20-way "which clause type does this passage contain?" question), with option
    descriptions taken from CUAD's clause-category descriptions.
  - The gold answer is derived from CUAD's human labels; no label was changed or
    generated by a model.
  - The run records add model responses, probabilities, latencies and costs
    produced by NXTG.AI's evaluation runs.

The CUAD-derived data is provided under CC BY 4.0, not under Apache-2.0.
NXTG.AI's own additions to the data files (questions, metadata, model outputs)
are also released under CC BY 4.0.

